.Dd May 5, 2026
.Dt PLAKAR-TUI 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm plakar-tui
.Nd Browse a Plakar repository in a terminal user interface
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm plakar tui
.Op Fl no-highlight
.Op Ar snapshot Ar path
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm plakar tui
command opens an interactive terminal user interface to browse a Plakar
repository.
It provides a dashboard with repository statistics, a list of snapshots,
and a file browser to navigate the contents of a snapshot.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl no-highlight
Disable syntax highlighting when displaying file contents.
.El
.Pp
If
.Ar snapshot
is provided, the file browser opens directly on that snapshot.
.Ar path
may be a path relative to the snapshot root or an absolute path within it.
.Pp
Keys:
.Bl -tag -width "pgup/pgdn"
.It Li q
Quit.
.It Li s
Open the snapshot list from the dashboard.
.It Li enter
Open the selected snapshot or file.
.It Li up , down
Move the selection.
.It Li left , right
Change page in the snapshot list.
.It Li backspace
Go to the parent directory, or back to the previous view.
.It Li r
Refresh the current view.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Open the dashboard:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ plakar tui
.Ed
Open the file browser on a specific snapshot:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ plakar tui 1a2b3c4d
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr plakar 1 ,
.Xr plakar-cat 1 ,
.Xr plakar-ls 1 ,
.Xr plakar-ui 1
